<title>SINGAPORE: HBO to launch second movie channel in Asia.</title>
<headline>HBO to launch second movie channel in Asia.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Home Box Office (HBO) said on Tuesday it would launch a second movie channel in Asia from November 15.</p>
<p>The new 24-hour English-language channel, Cinemax, will be transmitted via the Apstar 1 satellite and will broadcast a wide selection of films, a statement by HBO said.</p>
<p>It said Cinemax would feature different genres of movies on different nights of the week.</p>
<p>Cinemax is the second pay-television service of HBO Pacific Partners, a joint venture of Time Warner Entertainment, Paramount Films, Sony Pictures Entertainment and MCA/Universal.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
